&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 72pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 108%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 108%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1) Assets recoverable without earning a return.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Our significant regulatory assets and liabilities include:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Taxes on capitalized funds used during construction. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the deferred income taxes on AFUDC equity funds. These amounts are recoverable in our tariff rates over the depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Income tax related. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the anticipated return to ratepayers of deferred income taxes as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, which lowered the U.S. federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% effective January 1, 2018. These amounts are amortized to Account 411.1 &amp;#8220;Provision for Deferred Income Taxes &amp;#8211; Credit&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Difference between gas retained and gas consumed in operations. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts reflect the value of the difference between the quantity of gas retained for fuel and lost and unaccounted for (L&amp;amp;U) and the quantity of gas consumed and L&amp;amp;U experienced in our operations. Pursuant to our tariff, the quantities associated with these amounts are expected to be recovered from or returned to our customers in subsequent periods. On a periodic basis, we file reports with the FERC detailing our volumetric fuel and L&amp;amp;U reimbursement activity and establishing prospective fuel and L&amp;amp;U retention rates. Volumetric over- or under-collections of fuel and L&amp;amp;U quantities from prior periods are trued up through either an addition or reduction to the prospective fuel and L&amp;amp;U retention rates. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded a net regulatory expense of $1.5 million and $1.2 million, respectively, related to our fuel and L&amp;amp;U activity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Revenue sharing. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Pursuant to our tariff, certain revenues from interruptible transportation services on our system are refundable to our shippers. We accrue for the refund as the interruptible transportation services are provided. Annually, our shippers receive an invoice credit for the refunded amount.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Electric power costs. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;We have a FERC approved tariff mechanism to track the electricity power costs at certain compressor stations and an amine gas processing facility on our system. On an annual basis, we file to update the prospective electric power cost charge. Our tariff provides that the difference between the amount of revenue received from the electric power cost charge and the amount of electric costs incurred over the applicable collection period be included in the calculation to update the electric power cost charge.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded a net regulatory expense of $0.4 million and $1.4 million, respectively, related to the provisions of this tracker.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7. Commitments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;We have a compression agreement and a capacity arrangement with our affiliates CIG and NGPL, respectively, resulting in commitments as of December 31, 2025 totaling $20.7 million. Our annual commitments under these agreements are $5.2 million for each of the years 2026 and 2027, $5.1 million for each of the years 2028 and 2029, and $0.1 million in 2030. During the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we incurred expenses of $5.2 million and $1.0 million, respectively, under these agreements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8. Recent Accounting Pronouncement&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;ASU No. 2025-06&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On September 18, 2025, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued ASU No. 2025-06, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;&amp;#8220;Intangibles&amp;#8212;Goodwill and Other&amp;#8212;Internal-Use Software (Subtopic 350-40): Targeted Improvements to the Accounting for Internal-Use Software.&amp;#8221;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; This ASU modernizes the accounting guidance for the costs to develop software for internal use by removing outdated stage-based cost capitalization rules and replacing them with a probability-based cost-capitalization framework that aligns better with current software development methods. This ASU will be effective for annual periods beginning after December 15, 2027, for interim reporting periods beginning within those annual periods, and early adoption is permitted. Management is currently evaluating this ASU to determine its impact on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:LessorName id="Tag1652" contextRef="C284">Natural Gas Pipeline Company of America LLC</ferc:LessorName>
  <ferc:IndicationOfAssociatedCompany id="Tag1653" contextRef="C284">true</ferc:IndicationOfAssociatedCompany>
  <ferc:LeaseDescription id="Tag1654" contextRef="C284">75,000 DTH/day leased capacity in approximately 200 miles of transmission  pipeline located at an interconnect point in Ford County, Kansas and the SPS Brickplant Road Delivery Point in Potter County, Texas</ferc:LeaseDescription>
  <ferc:GasPropertyAndCapacityLeasePayment id="Tag1655" contextRef="C284" unitRef="USD" decimals="0">4194000</ferc:GasPropertyAndCapacityLeasePayment>
  <ferc:GasPropertyAndCapacityLeasePayment id="Tag1656" contextRef="C1" unitRef="USD" decimals="0">4194000</ferc:GasPropertyAndCapacityLeasePayment>
  <ferc:OrderNumber id="Tag1657" contextRef="C284" unitRef="Pure" decimals="0">1</ferc:OrderNumber>
